# A `bytes` slice CLAMPS out-of-range bounds, it does not trap
# (docs/spec/03-types.md, the `b[i:j]` row). A parser must not use a slice as
# its bounds check: compare len() first. This fixture pins the clamp so a change
# to trapping cannot land silently.
fn main():
    b := to_bytes("abc")
    println(str(len(b[1:99])))
    println(str(len(b[9:99])))
    println(str(len(b[0:3])))
